    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "GC errors \u2014 ALERT IF INCREASING",
      "description": "offshoot_gc_errors_total: janitor GC passes that returned an error. GC fails CLOSED (an incomplete reachability mark deletes nothing), so a persistently increasing value means garbage is accumulating unreclaimed. The paired 'offshoot: janitor: gc:' stderr line carries the cause. This is the fail-closed alarm: alert on any increase.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
